# Testing

## API (`apps/api`)

- **Framework**: Jest + `@nestjs/testing` + supertest
- **Unit**: `src/**/*.spec.ts` co-located
- **E2E**: `test/**/*.e2e-spec.ts` — assert status codes, headers, JSON body
- **Run**: `pnpm test:api`, `pnpm test:api:e2e`
- REST: e2e must verify correct HTTP method, status, and response shape

## Web (`apps/web`)

- **Framework**: Vitest + React Testing Library + `@testing-library/user-event`
- **Location**: `ComponentName.test.tsx` beside `ComponentName.tsx`
- **Run**: `pnpm test:web` (from root, when configured)
- **Required**: every component under `components/` has a test file before merge

### Essential usage (web)

Cover at minimum: render smoke, main interaction, critical text/role. Skip implementation details (class names, internal state).

```tsx
// ✅ Essential usage
describe('Button', () => {
  it('renders label', () => {
    render(<Button>Save</Button>)
    expect(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /save/i })).toBeInTheDocument()
  })
})
```

- ❌ New component without `.test.tsx`
- ❌ Testing Tailwind class strings instead of behavior/accessibility
